(1) The amended provisions of the latter part of Article 133-2 (1) shall also apply to the corrections made to a patent of which a trial on invalidation is pending as at the time this Act enters into force.
(2) The following amended provisions shall apply the requests filed to correct the specification or drawings of a patented invention after this Act enters into force:
1. The amended provisions of the former part of Article 133-2 (4) (limited to the part to which the amended proviso of Article 136 (8) shall apply mutatis mutandis);
2. The amended provisions of the latter part of Article 133-2 (4) (limited to the amended part regarding Article 133-2 (1));
3. The amended provisions of Article 133-2 (5).
Article 12 (Applicability to Consent to Petitions for Trial on Correction)
The amended provisions of Article 136 (8) and (9) shall apply to the trials on correction for which a petition is filed after this Act enters into force.
Article 13 (Applicability to Trials to Invalidate Corrections)
(1) The amended provisions of the latter part of Article 137 (3) shall also apply to the trials pending on invalidation of corrections as at the time this Act enters into force.
(2) The amended provisions of Article 137 (4) (limited to the part to which the following amended provisions shall apply mutatis mutandis) shall apply the requests filed to correct the specification or drawings of a patented invention after this Act enters into force:
1. The amended provisions of the former part of Article 133-2 (4) (limited to the part to which the amended proviso of Article 136 (8) shall apply mutatis mutandis);
2. The amended provisions of the latter part of Article 133-2 (4) (limited to the amended part regarding Article 133-2 (1));
3. The amended provisions of Article 133-2 (5).
Article 14 (Applicability to Dismissal of Petitions for Trial)
The amended provisions of Article 141 (2) shall apply to the trials for which a petition is filed after this Act enters into force.
Article 15 (Applicability to Application Mutatis Mutandis of Examination-Related Provisions to Trial on Ruling Rejecting Patent Applications)
The amended provisions of Article 170 (1) (limited to the amended part related to Article 47 (4)) shall also apply to amendments to patent applications regarding which a trial on a ruling to reject a patent application is pending as at the time this Act enters into force.
Article 16 (Transitional Measure concerning Request for Extending Period for Filing Petition for Trial on Decision to Reject Patent Applications)
A person who filed a request for extending the period for filing a petition for trial with respect to a decision to reject a patent application or a decision to reject extended registration of the period of existence of a patent with the President of the Korean Intellectual Property Trial and Appeal Board pursuant to the previous main clause of Article 15 (1) before this Act enters into force shall be deemed to have filed the request with the Commissioner of the Korean Intellectual Property Office.
Article 17 (Transitional Measure concerning Subsequent Completion of Procedure)
Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 17, the previous provisions shall apply where the period during which the procedure can be subsequently completed in accordance with the previous provisions as at the time this Act enters into force has already passed.
Article 18 (Transitional Measure concerning Retroactive Filing Date of Patent Applications by Legitimate Right Holders)
Notwithstanding the amended proviso of Article 35, the previous provisions shall apply to an unentitled person's patent the grant of which has been registered before this Act enters into force.
Article 19 (Transitional Measure concerning Period for Requesting Examination of Patent Applications)
Notwithstanding the amended provisions of the main clause of Article 59 (2), the previous provisions shall apply to the patent applications filed before this Act enters into force.
Article 20 (Transitional Measure concerning Ex Officio Amendments)
Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 66-2, the previous provisions shall apply where the specification, drawings, or abstract that accompanies a patent application was amended ex officio before this Act enters into force.
Article 21 (Transitional Measure concerning Trial on Invalidity of Patents)
Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 133 (1), the previous provisions shall apply to patents the grant of which has been registered before this Act enters into force.
Article 22 (Transitional Measure concerning Permission for Inspection of Documents)
Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 216 (2), the previous provisions shall apply to earlier applications filed before this Act enters into force, on which the priority claim under Article 55 (1) is based.
Article 23 Omitted.

