Article 1 (Enforcement Date)
This Act shall enter into force six months after the date of its promulgation.
Article 3 (Applicability to Invalidation of Procedures)
The amended provisions of Article 16 (2) shall also apply where patent-related procedures are invalidated because a person who was ordered to make an amendment before entry into force of this Act has failed to observe the period of amendment for good cause, in which case two months have not elapsed from the date such grounds cease to exist as at the time this Act enters into force.
Article 3 (Applicability to Divisional Applications)
(1) The amended provisions of Article 52 (1) shall begin to apply to divisional applications based on the patent application regarding which a certified copy of the decision to reject the patent is served after this Act enters into force.
(2) The amended provisions of Article 52 (4) and (5) shall begin to apply to divisional applications filed after this Act enters into force.
Article 4 (Applicability to Splitting-Off)
The amended provisions of Article 52-2 shall begin to apply to where patent applications for which a request for trial against a decision to reject a patent application is filed after this Act enters into force, are split off.
Article 5 (Applicability to Converted Applications)
The amended provisions of Article 53 (1) shall begin to apply to converted applications based on application for registration of a utility model regarding which a certified copy of a decision to reject utility model registration is served after this Act enters into force.
Article 6 (Applicability to Priority Claims Based on Patent Applications)
The amended provisions of Articles 55 (1) 4 and (8) and 56 (1) 2 shall begin to apply to priority claims filed based on the earlier applications regarding which the certified copy of a decision to grant a patent under Article 66 after this Act enters into force; of a decision to register a utility model under Article 66 of the Patent Act applied mutatis mutandis pursuant to Article 15 of the Utility Model Act; or of a decision to revoke a decision to refuse to register a utility model under Article 176 (1) of the Patent Act applied mutatis mutandis pursuant to Article 33 of the Utility Model Act (limited to a trial decision to register a patent or a utility model, but including a trial decision on retrial).
Article 7 (Applicability to Request for Re-Examination)
The amended provisions of Article 67-2 (1) and (3) shall begin to apply to patent applications regarding which the certified copy of a written decision to grant a patent under Article 66 or the certified copy of a trial decision to revoke the decision to reject a patent application under Article 176 (1) (limited to a trial decision made to register a patent but including a trial decision on retrial) is served after this Act enters into force.
Article 8 (Applicability to Reinstatement of Patent Applications)
The amended provisions of Article 67-3 (1) shall also apply where a patent application is deemed withdrawn or a decision to reject a patent is deemed made final and conclusive because a patent applicant fails to comply with any of the periods under the subparagraphs of the same paragraph for good cause before entry into force of this Act and where two months have not passed from the date such grounds cease to exist.
Article 9 (Applicability to Reinstatement of Patent Applications or Patents by Making Late Payment of Patent Fees or Payment of Under-Paid Patent Fees)
The amended provisions of Article 81-3 (1) shall also apply where a person who intends to obtain grant of a patent registered before entry into force of this Act, or where a patentee fails to pay a patent fee within the period for payment of patent fees due to good cause or to pay an under-paid patent fee during the period for payment within such period, and two months have not passed from the date such grounds cease to exist as at the time this Act entered into force.
Article 10 (Applicability to Non-Exclusive Licenses Subsequent to Transfer of Patents by Exercise of Pledge Rights)
The amended provisions of Article 122 shall begin to apply to cases where a request for the division of a jointly owned patent is filed after this Act enters into force.
Article 11 (Applicability to Trial on Rulings Rejecting Patent Applications)
The amended provisions of Article 132-17 shall begin to apply to patent applications on which a certified copy of the decision to reject a patent application or a certified copy of the decision to reject an application to register the extended term a patent is served after this Act enters into force.
Article 12 Omitted.
Article 13 (Applicability Following Amendments to Other Statutes)
The amended provisions of Article 10 (1) 1 of the Utility Model Act amended pursuant to Article 12 of the Addenda shall begin to apply to converted applications based on patent applications for which a certified copy of the decision to reject a patent application is served after this Act enters into force.

